  "issue": {
    "id": "I_kwDOAd1its7cbiYC",
    "databaseId": 3698206210,
    "number": 1775,
    "title": "Unable to install ros-humble-librealsense2 DEB package on systems with automounted homes",
    "url": "https://github.com/ros2/ros2/issues/1775",
    "body": "### Generated by Generative AI\n\nno\n\n### Operating System:\n\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS\n\n### ROS version or commit hash:\n\nhumble\n\n### RMW implementation (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### RMW Configuration (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client library (if applicable):\n\n_No response_\n\n### 'ros2 doctor --report' output\n\n\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce issue\n\n1. Run `sudo apt-get install ros-humble-librealsense2`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should install the library as expected.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nOn a system that has NFS-mounted homes, the installation fails:\n\n```\nUnpacking ros-humble-librealsense2 (2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252) ...\ndpkg: error processing archive /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb (--unpack):\n error creating directory './home/buildfarm': Permission denied\ndpkg-deb: error: paste subprocess was killed by signal (Broken pipe)\nErrors were encountered while processing:\n /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb\nE: Sub-process /usr/bin/dpkg returned an error code (1)\n```\n\n\n### Additional information\n\nThe package contains a file named `/home/buildfarm/Documents/librealsense2/presets/sample.preset`. It doesn't make any sense for a package to create a directory in `/home` and even less one that doesn't correspond to an actual account. This file possibly belongs in /usr/share/doc.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Generated by Generative AI</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">no</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Operating System:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Ubuntu 22.04 LTS</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">ROS version or commit hash:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">humble</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW implementation (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">RMW Configuration (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Client library (if applicable):</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><em>No response</em></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">'ros2 doctor --report' output</h3>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Steps to reproduce issue</h3>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Run <code class=\"notranslate\">sudo apt-get install ros-humble-librealsense2</code></li>\n</ol>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Expected behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It should install the library as expected.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Actual behavior</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">On a system that has NFS-mounted homes, the installation fails:</p>\n<div class=\"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"Unpacking ros-humble-librealsense2 (2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252) ...\ndpkg: error processing archive /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb (--unpack):\n error creating directory './home/buildfarm': Permission denied\ndpkg-deb: error: paste subprocess was killed by signal (Broken pipe)\nErrors were encountered while processing:\n /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb\nE: Sub-process /usr/bin/dpkg returned an error code (1)\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Unpacking ros-humble-librealsense2 (2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252) ...\ndpkg: error processing archive /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb (--unpack):\n error creating directory './home/buildfarm': Permission denied\ndpkg-deb: error: paste subprocess was killed by signal (Broken pipe)\nErrors were encountered while processing:\n /var/cache/apt/archives/ros-humble-librealsense2_2.56.4-1jammy.20250722.184252_amd64.deb\nE: Sub-process /usr/bin/dpkg returned an error code (1)\n</code></pre></div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional information</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The package contains a file named <code class=\"notranslate\">/home/buildfarm/Documents/librealsense2/presets/sample.preset</code>. It doesn't make any sense for a package to create a directory in <code class=\"notranslate\">/home</code> and even less one that doesn't correspond to an actual account. This file possibly belongs in /usr/share/doc.</p>",
